course: dictionary
lesson: 12952
title: Too much, and past a sensible limit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how much or how far. Excessively is one of them. It means too much, more than is normal, needed or healthy. «Ben played games excessively, so he was too tired for school.» The word tells you that Ben did not play a little. He played past the point where it was good for him.
explain: Look at what the word is joined to. «The soup was excessively salty, so nobody could eat it.» Salty alone is a taste. Excessively salty means there was far too much salt. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The soup was far too much salty» sounds odd, but «The soup was far too salty» works, so excessively is saying the same thing as far too.
explain: In health lessons this word is a warning. «Eating excessively sugary food can rot your teeth.» Some things are fine in small amounts but harmful in large amounts. Excessively tells you the amount has gone past a sensible limit.
fact: Excessively is an adverb, so it tells you more about how something is done or how much it is.
fact: Excessively means too much, more than is normal, needed or healthy.
fact: In formal writing, excessively often means «far too».
fact: Common phrases: excessively hot, excessively long, drink excessively.
fact: «Excessively» is a word for amounts that have gone past a sensible limit, so it is often used when something might be harmful.
exercise: «The soup was excessively salty.» What does excessively mean here? | A little bit salty | Not salty at all | Sweet and sour | *Far too much salt
exercise: Which phrase means the same as excessively hot? | Just right for a bath | *Far too hot | A little warm | Cool and calm
exercise: «Eating excessively sugary food is bad for your teeth.» Why is this bad? | *Because too much sugar is harmful | Because sugar makes teeth shiny | Because sugar is a kind of food | Because teeth like sweet things
test: «Sam drank excessively fizzy juice at the party.» What does excessively tell you about the juice? | *He drank far more than was healthy | He did not drink any | He drank it very slowly | It was just the right amount
test: Which sentence uses excessively correctly to mean too much? | «He wrote excessively with a pencil.» | «She ran excessively to the shop and back in one minute.» | *«The film was excessively long for a young child.» | «The sun is excessively in the sky.»
exam: Which word means the same as excessively in «The water was excessively cold»? | Pleasantly | Gently | *Far too | Slightly
